  <questionvariables><text><![CDATA[/* Fixed: one specific proof. The best summary is second. */
ta1: [
 [s_check, false, "Check that \\(n^2 - 1\\) is a multiple of 8 for \\(n = 1, 3, 5, 7\\) and \\(9\\), and conclude that it is a multiple of 8 for every odd number \\(n\\)."],
 [s_pair, true, "Write \\(n = 2k + 1\\), so that \\(n^2 - 1 = 4k(k + 1)\\). One of the consecutive integers \\(k\\) and \\(k + 1\\) is even, so \\(n^2 - 1\\) is 8 times an integer."],
 [s_four, false, "Write \\(n = 2k + 1\\), so that \\(n^2 - 1 = 4k^2 + 4k\\). This is a multiple of 4, and so it is also a multiple of 8 for every odd \\(n\\)."],
 [s_parity, false, "Since \\(n\\) is odd, \\(n^2\\) is odd, so \\(n^2 - 1\\) is even. Every even number is a multiple of 8, so \\(n^2 - 1\\) is a multiple of 8."]
];]]></text></questionvariables>
